.TH GPS-TOF-NOTE-TABLES 1 "2026-11-06" "gps-tof 0.7.0" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
make_note_tables.py \- generate the LaTeX tables of the technical note from the JSON report
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B python3 scripts/make_note_tables.py
[\fB\-\-json\fR \fIreports/nova.json\fR] [\fB\-\-out\fR \fIdocs/note/generated\fR]
.SH DESCRIPTION
Reads the JSON report written by \fBgps-tof -c config/nova.yaml -f json\fR and writes one
LaTeX fragment per table of \fIdocs/note/nova-tof-note.tex\fR (input positions, survey points,
converted positions, chords by Earth model, correction ledgers, chord geometry, flight times,
Main Injector shift, combined offset, trigger window, non-geometric effects, beam-axis
quantities, opening angles, face edges, validation, sensitivities, error budget, the
reproduction of the 2013 notebook and the history of the ND/FD geometries).  Every number in
the note therefore comes from the code; edit the configuration, rerun gps-tof, rerun this
script and rebuild the note.  Table bodies end with their own \\bottomrule because a rule
placed after \\input in the including file breaks LaTeX's row scanning.
.SH BUILDING THE NOTE
.nf
    gps-tof -c config/nova.yaml -f all -o reports/nova
    python3 scripts/make_note_tables.py
    cd docs/note && latexmk -pdf nova-tof-note        # or: make
.fi
Figures come from \fIdocs/figures/*.svg\fR converted to PDF in \fIdocs/note/figures/\fR
(see \fBgps-tof-export-figures\fR(1)).
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR gps-tof (1),
.BR gps-tof-export-figures (1)
